<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 88,103 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 88,103 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 88,103 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Thursday compared to 59,836 tonnes in the same period on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Thursday    Jan 29</p>
<p>    Export cargo		 7,938	 8,805</p>
<p>    Import cargo		80,165	51,031</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, three are expected to sail and 10 are expected to arrive.</p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Palm oil		 15,000	 Wawasan Megah     30/1</p>
<p>Gas oil		  35,000	 Rose Bud	    30/1</p>
<p>High speed diesel    73,000	 Chesa Peak City    1/2</p>
<p>Crude oil		71,000	 Stavros-1	    2/2</p>
<p>Jet oil		  25,000	 Ras Al-Zour	  3/2</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Wawasan Courage    5/2</p>
<p>High speed diesel    56,000	 Keefan		 7/2</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
